<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE ussf-266 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>RETIMED 2026-11-24 (board ~16:00Z): T0 is the window open 2026-11-24T16:08:59Z (+839 s from 2026-11-24T15:55:00Z), four-hour window to 2026-11-24T20:08:59Z. Live LL2 id 460d9db7-eaf6-4cd9-b095-cff433534c09 re-queried this run: status Go for Launch, net 2026-11-24T16:08:59Z, second precision, last_updated 2026-11-24T15:56:16Z. Not launched. LL2 window_start and window_end are still 2026-11-24T15:55:00Z and 2026-11-24T19:55:00Z. SpaceX page: four-hour window opens at 8:08 a.m. PT (https://www.spacex.com/launches/ussf266), which is 16:08Z; the close used here is that open plus four hours, 20:08:59Z, not LL2&#x27;s 19:55Z. Backup still Wednesday 25 Nov 7:46 a.m. PT (2026-11-25T15:46:00Z). utc shifted +839 s. ECEF geometry unchanged. Sim not re-run. ILLUSTRATIVE.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 USSF-266 (SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
TIMELINE mode: every ignition/cutoff/separation/fairing time is a published hard event; mdot=F_vac/(Isp_vac*g0); thrust SL/vac on ambient pressure.
FITTED (least squares vs published knots): vertical rise 10.16 s, kick 3.807 deg over 10 s, Cd 0.400, payload 15021 kg,
gravity turn, then linear-tangent steering tan(theta)=0.5561-0.001364*(t-t_ign stage 1).
Vehicle config: SpaceX Falcon 9 Block 5 (reusable first stage, droneship recovery) — TIMELINE mode (sim/vehicles/falcon9.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Falcon 9 Block 5 masses from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9 Block 5&#x27; spec table; thrust/Isp from Wikipedia &#x27;Falcon 9&#x27; spec table (citing SpaceX).
TIMELINE mode (tuned 2026-10-25): MECO 146 s, stage sep 150 s, SES-1 156 s, fairing 176 s, SECO-1 (final cutoff) from SpaceX&#x27;s sl-15-16 timeline are hard events.
Throttle profile not published: full published thrust throughout; unburned stage-1 residual stands in for entry/landing propellant.
ILLUSTRATIVE. PRE-FLIGHT. USSF-266, Falcon 9, SLC-4E. T0 is the window open 2026-11-24T15:55:00Z (Tue 24 Nov 7:55 a.m. PT). SpaceX https://www.spacex.com/launches/ussf266: four-hour window to 19:55Z. Backup Wed 25 Nov 7:46 a.m. PT = 2026-11-25T15:46:00Z. 29th flight of the first stage. Landing on Of Course I Still Love You. LL2 id 460d9db7-eaf6-4cd9-b095-cff433534c09 status Go at 15:55Z.
Published timeline (SpaceX ussf266): Max-Q 1:07, MECO 2:26, stage sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:56, entry burn 6:03-6:27, landing burn 8:01, landing 8:23. SECO, orbit and deploy are not published. Payload is classified. No unofficial satellite count is used.
AZIMUTH CONFLICT recorded, not averaged. NOTAM MMFO B4504/26 is the stage-1 reentry box (centroid bearing about 169.4 deg, 672 km). A constant-azimuth rhumb at 193.41 deg does not pass through that box (about 280 km cross-track at 670 km). The stage-1 box was not used for the azimuth, the same rule as NROL-136. Its 24 Nov period is 1555-2038Z, the older FAA backup close, not the current 1955Z window close.
INFERRED/ASSUMED: SECO-1 at T+519 s and a 177 x 266 km parking orbit are borrowed from the sl-15-16 / Group 15 family, not from USSF-266. File ends 2 revs after cutoff (deploy unpublished). Booster entry and landing are not modelled.
Target (see launch config): insertion 177 km, apoapsis 266 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 193.41 deg; payload 15021 kg.
Pad: 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-24T16:08:59Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (SpaceX publishes no SECO, restart or deploy time for USSF-266 (classified payload). Propagated 2 revs on the inferred insertion orbit. The insertion altitude is borrowed, not a USSF-266 element.). From insertion T+519.0 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 88.93 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF end T+11191 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 177.28 km, osculating 174.7 x 268.7 km, i 99.47 deg.</description>
